# Line endings are pinned here on purpose.
#
# Windows Git checks out text files with CRLF by default. A shell script with
# CRLF endings fails inside a Linux container with a misleading error:
#
#   exec /app/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# ...because Linux looks for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r".
#
# See WSL2-NOTES.md #2. Day 2 makes you trigger this on purpose so you
# recognise it forever.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles must never be CRLF, no exceptions.
*.sh      text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.conf    text eol=lf

# Binary files must not be touched at all.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.gz      binary
*.tar     binary
